== Usage ==
*<pvxbig> 
* Build enough adrenaline with your Spear and keep {{skill pvxicon|Rending Aura|6}} active.
* It is recommended to wait till Rending Aura is off cooldown for maximum effectiveness.
* With {{skill pvxicon|Rending Aura|6}} active, spike with {{skill pvxicon|Reaper's Sweep|9}} → cancel action (default key: Escape) → switch to dagger set → {{skill pvxicon|Rending Aura|6}} + {{skill pvxicon|Heart of Fury|0}} + {{skill pvxicon|Falling Lotus Strike|14}} → {{skill pvxicon|Twisting Fangs|8}} → {{skill pvxicon|Falling Spider|14}} → {{skill pvxicon|Blades of Steel|14}}.
** If fearing the combo will fail, skip one of the dual attacks.
* Inbetween spikes, use {{skill pvxicon|Reaper's Sweep|9}} → cancel action (default key: Escape) → switch to dagger set → {{skill pvxicon|Rending Aura|6}} → {{skill pvxicon|Falling Spider|14}} → {{skill pvxicon|Blades of Steel|14}} for a mini-spike.

== Counters ==
* Anti-melee
* Heavy enchantment removal;
* Knock-down protection

== Notes ==
* The spike combo requires very tight timing
** Heart of Fury cannot be pressed too early before Falling Lotus, otherwise Falling Spider won't benefit from the IAS and will miss the knockdown state
** At the same time, Falling Lotus Strike cannot be activated too late after Reaper's Sweep, or Falling Spider will miss as well
** It takes a good amount of time practicing to get the timing right.
** As a result, the build is not recommended when playing with very high ping. </pvxbig>